  "scope": "The upstream CMake library source list is generated with Fypp 3.2, with every generated file checksum locked in the recipe. The example exercises communicator initialization, real-vector broadcast, real and integer all-reduce and in-place maximum reduction on exactly one MPI process, checking API statuses and returned data. MPICH is pinned and UCX transports are limited to self/shared memory. This illustrates typed communication APIs, not parallel execution or speedup; point-to-point messaging, multiple processes and other wrappers are outside verification scope. Classification R covers the tested service routines.",
  "generation_note": "Fypp 3.2 output checksums were independently reproduced on Linux/Python 3.12 from the pinned templates. LF text normalization keeps hashes identical on Windows and Linux.",
  "runtime_note": "The checked example uses one MPI process. UCX emits a network-discovery diagnostic about /sys/class/net, which the restricted gVisor sandbox does not expose. The program exits successfully and all data/numerical checks pass. The diagnostic is retained verbatim in verified-output.txt."
